## Root cause
`/dayjs/src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js` hardcoded English meridiem handling: the `A`/`a` tokens used `matchUpperCaseAMPM = /[AP]M/` and `matchLowerCaseAMPM = /[ap]m/`, and their parsers did `this.afternoon = input === 'PM'` / `input === 'pm'`. Any non-English meridiem string (zh-cn 上午/下午, ja 午前/午後, ko 오전/오후, br a.m./g.m.) therefore never matched the regex, so `match[0]` was undefined → `parser.call` threw → `parseFormattedInput` returned `new Date('')` (Invalid Date). Reproduced empirically before fixing: 8/12 scratch cases failed (all non-English locales), 4 English cases passed.

