`matchWord` (already used by `MMM`/`MMMM`/`Do`) captures the locale meridiem token; `meridiemMatch` scans hours 1..24 with `locale.meridiem(i, 0, isLowerCase)` (last match wins, so multi-hour spans like zh-cn 上午 = hours 9–11 and 下午 = 13–17 resolve correctly) and falls back to the original English `'PM'`/`'pm'` comparison for locales without `meridiem` (e.g. `en`, `ru`). `correctHours` is untouched.

